                                                                            <comments>
                            <comment id="493481" author="adilger" created="Tue, 21 Apr 2026 08:06:46 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;This should probably use the new scanning callback function implemented in patch &lt;a href=&quot;https://review.whamcloud.com/63165&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://review.whamcloud.com/63165&lt;/a&gt; (&quot;&lt;tt&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-19598&quot; title=&quot;TCU: Clean up files from the Trash Can&quot; class=&quot;issue-link&quot; data-issue-key=&quot;LU-19598&quot;&gt;LU-19598&lt;/a&gt; utils: add a new API llapi_find_with_cb()&lt;/tt&gt;&quot;).&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="495345" author="gerrit" created="Mon, 1 Jun 2026 18:28:04 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;&quot;Chakshu Kansal &amp;lt;ckansal@ddn.com&amp;gt;&quot; uploaded a new patch: &lt;a href=&quot;https://review.whamcloud.com/c/fs/lustre-release/+/66408&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://review.whamcloud.com/c/fs/lustre-release/+/66408&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br/&gt;
Subject: &lt;a href=&quot;https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-19125&quot; title=&quot; move &amp;quot;lfs project&amp;quot; over to parallel &amp;quot;lfs find&amp;quot; infrastructure&quot; class=&quot;issue-link&quot; data-issue-key=&quot;LU-19125&quot;&gt;LU-19125&lt;/a&gt; lfs: add multithreading to lfs project command&lt;br/&gt;
Project: fs/lustre-release&lt;br/&gt;
Branch: master&lt;br/&gt;
Current Patch Set: 1&lt;br/&gt;
Commit: 50f056defec181c09a440d84db61f0f08d80e2d1&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="495370" author="adilger" created="Tue, 2 Jun 2026 07:25:08 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;It&apos;s worthwhile to note that it is possible to implement parallel scanning on a single directory by splitting up the 2^63 directory hash cookie into N (or 2N or similar) ranges and then have each thread call &lt;tt&gt;telldir()&lt;/tt&gt; to their relative offset and then call &lt;tt&gt;readdir()&lt;/tt&gt; until the returned entry hash hits the start of the next window..&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
